-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party work
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Rematch builds on the work below. Each item keeps its own licence. Nothing in
this list is relicensed by the AGPL. The web app shows the full texts of the
parts it ships to the browser at /licenses (apps/web/src/app/licenses/texts.ts).

Engines and data (run on the server, not committed to this repository)

  Stockfish 19
    https://github.com/official-stockfish/Stockfish
    Copyright (C) 2004-2026 The Stockfish developers (see the AUTHORS file in its source)
    Licence: GNU General Public License v3.0 (GPL-3.0-or-later)
    The official release binary is downloaded at image build time and checked
    against a pinned SHA-256 (apps/worker/Dockerfile, backend/Dockerfile). It
    runs unmodified, as a separate process. Its source is at the URL above.

  Maia-2 (optional, only with docker-compose.maia.yml)
    https://github.com/CSSLab/maia2
    Copyright (c) 2024 CSSLab
    Licence: MIT. The model weights are fetched by the maia2 package at image
    build time and SHA-256 verified; they are never committed (ADR-R2-13).
    Inside that optional image, python-chess is GPL-3.0-or-later, and certifi
    and tqdm are MPL-2.0. They are installed unmodified from PyPI.

  Syzygy 3-4-5 piece endgame tablebases
    Fetched from the Lichess tablebase mirror (https://tablebase.lichess.ovh/)
    and SHA-256 verified against a pinned manifest; never committed
    (ADR-R2-22). The tables are computed data and the mirror asserts no
    restrictive licence. The generator (syzygy1/tb, GPL-2.0, by Ronald de Man)
    is not used or distributed here.

  Opening names: lichess-org/chess-openings
    https://github.com/lichess-org/chess-openings
    Dedicated to the public domain under CC0 1.0 Universal.

